  "records": {
    "description": "A 32x32 screen that allows you to set pixel to 1 or 0, fill the screen with 1 or 0, and draw a 4x6 sprite at any coordinate. It has a buffer.",
    "input": "- pixel x (5 bit)\n- pixel y (5 bit)\n- sprite x (5 bit)\n- sprite y (5 bit)\n- sprite input (6 nibble)\n- draw sprite\n- pixel color\n- draw pixel\n- fill screen\n- buffer",
    "output": "Lamps",
    "speed": "Draws sprite in 4rt (6 pixels / 1rt)",
    "notes": "- (0, 0) is in the top left corner.\n- Sprite coordinate specifies the bottom left corner of the sprite, so if you want to draw full 4x6 sprite in top left corner, sprite coordinate should be (0, 5)."
  },
